Bug found and fixed. The issue was on line 7 of `src/import_merge.ts`:

**Before:** `const match = result.find((b) => b.url === inc.url);`
**After:** `const match = result.find((b) => b.url.toLowerCase() === inc.url.toLowerCase());`

The original code used strict string equality (`===`) to match URLs, which is case-sensitive. URLs with different hostname casing (e.g., `https://example.com/a` vs `https://EXAMPLE.com/a`) were treated as different URLs, causing the incoming bookmark to be added as a duplicate instead of being merged.

The fix normalizes both URLs to lowercase before comparison, so hostname case differences no longer prevent proper merging. Tags from both entries are still unioned as before. Lint check passes.


